{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01WG78H6a26wx3kVyWMHN2p9", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orang_Rimba_people\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kubu_language\"}, {\"url\": \"https://Www.Wikipedia.org/wiki/Kubu_people\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.locjkt.or.id/application/docliblcjkt/upload/organisasi%20sosial%20dan.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://eprints.umk.ac.id/15933/3/Bab%201%20-%20BOOK%20CHAPTER%20WOMEN%20IN%20SOCIAL%20AND%20CULTURE-5-17.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://repository.isi-padangpanjang.ac.id/249/3/BAB%20I.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://factsanddetails.com/indonesia/Minorities_and_Regions/sub6_3b/entry-10144.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.tempo.co/amp/532462/into-the-wild\"}, {\"url\": \"https://journal.isi.ac.id/index.php/resital/article/download/489/83\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:27:36.545Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Orang Rimba Kubu menangkap kura-kura alat tradisional", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_013vaBo7xstmCvZo13b3HK2x", "content": [{"title": "Orang Rimba people", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orang_Rimba_people"}, {"title": "Kubu language", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kubu_language"}, {"title": "Orang Rimba people", "url": "https://Www.Wikipedia.org/wiki/Kubu_people"}, {"title": "www.locjkt.or.id", "url": "https://www.locjkt.or.id/application/docliblcjkt/upload/organisasi%20sosial%20dan.pdf"}, {"title": "Bab%201%20 %20BOOK%20CHAPTER%20WOMEN%20IN%20SOCIAL%20AND%20CULTURE 5 17", "url": "https://eprints.umk.ac.id/15933/3/Bab%201%20-%20BOOK%20CHAPTER%20WOMEN%20IN%20SOCIAL%20AND%20CULTURE-5-17.pdf"}, {"title": "repository.isi-padangpanjang.ac.id", "url": "https://repository.isi-padangpanjang.ac.id/249/3/BAB%20I.pdf"}, {"title": "ORANG RIMBA: FOREST, MARRIAGE, VILLAGERS, DEFORESTATION", "url": "https://factsanddetails.com/indonesia/Minorities_and_Regions/sub6_3b/entry-10144.html"}, {"title": "Into the Wild", "url": "https://en.tempo.co/amp/532462/into-the-wild"}, {"title": "journal.isi.ac.id", "url": "https://journal.isi.ac.id/index.php/resital/article/download/489/83"}]}, "The search didn't turn up anything specific about Orang Rimba (Kubu) catching turtles with traditional tools. The results cover their general background, not their hunting or fishing methods.\n\nWhat the results do say:\n\n- **Who they are:** The Orang Batin Sembilan, Orang Rimba, or Anak Dalam are mobile, animist peoples who live throughout the lowland forests of southeast Sumatra.\n- **Livelihood:** Their traditional way of life centers on hunting and gathering food while moving from place to place. That reliance on forest resources is why the results describe them as dependent on forest produce and game.\n- **Name:** \"Kubu\" is a Malay term that outsiders use for them, and it carries negative connotations, according to the results.\n\nFor the turtle question, I'd suggest searching in Indonesian for terms like \"Suku Anak Dalam berburu kura-kura\" or \"Orang Rimba tradisional perangkap hewan,\" or checking ethnographic studies of Jambi's Bukit Dua Belas area."], "durationSeconds": 5.172914749999998, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01WG78H6a26wx3kVyWMHN2p9", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01F6JtMMwXZTCQZiga3LEcSe", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orang_Rimba_people\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.thejakartapost.com/news/2009/09/09/kubu-tribespeople-struggle-without-traditions\"}, {\"url\": \"https://jurnal.harianregional.com/blje/id-98\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.everyculture.com/East-Southeast-Asia/Kubu.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/kubu\"}, {\"url\": \"https://dice.missouri.edu/assets/docs/austronesia/Kubu.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://Www.Wikipedia.org/wiki/Kubu_people\"}, {\"url\": \"https://asianethnology.org/article/1660/download\"}, {\"url\": \"https://asianethnology.org/article/1499/download\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.britannica.com/topic/Kubu\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:27:36.714Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Kubu tribe Sumatra traditional tool catch turtles", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01FDqoUJZtvfdMrEu3BtLBx5", "content": [{"title": "Orang Rimba people", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orang_Rimba_people"}, {"title": "kubu tribespeople struggle without traditions", "url": "https://www.thejakartapost.com/news/2009/09/09/kubu-tribespeople-struggle-without-traditions"}, {"title": "id 98", "url": "https://jurnal.harianregional.com/blje/id-98"}, {"title": "www.everyculture.com", "url": "https://www.everyculture.com/East-Southeast-Asia/Kubu.html"}, {"title": "www.encyclopedia.com", "url": "https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/kubu"}, {"title": "dice.missouri.edu", "url": "https://dice.missouri.edu/assets/docs/austronesia/Kubu.pdf"}, {"title": "Orang Rimba people", "url": "https://Www.Wikipedia.org/wiki/Kubu_people"}, {"title": "asianethnology.org", "url": "https://asianethnology.org/article/1660/download"}, {"title": "asianethnology.org", "url": "https://asianethnology.org/article/1499/download"}, {"title": "britannica.com", "url": "https://www.britannica.com/topic/Kubu"}]}, "The search didn't turn up any source describing a specific traditional tool the Kubu use to catch turtles. The results do confirm some related context:\n\n- **Turtle hunting is permitted:** Kubu living in Bukit Duabelas and Tigapuluh National Parks are allowed to hunt for boars and turtles, according to an NGO figure cited by the Jakarta Post. The article doesn't say how they catch them.\n- **Subsistence context:** The Orang Rimba combine hunting, trapping, fishing, and the collection of forest products for trade, per Wikipedia. Turtle-specific methods aren't described.\n- **Lifestyle has changed:** Encyclopedia.com notes that the traditional hunter-gatherer way of life is largely a thing of the past.\n\nTerminology is also worth knowing: \"Kubu\" is an outsider label, and Kubu groups themselves prefer to be called \"Orang Rimba\" (people of the forest).\n\nTo find the tool itself, a search for Orang Rimba or Orang Batin Sembilan hunting methods, or for ethnographic accounts from the Dutch colonial period (e.g., Van Dongen or Keereweer), would be a better next step."], "durationSeconds": 5.121199209000002, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01F6JtMMwXZTCQZiga3LEcSe", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
